Linux input methods for Godot 4.8-beta5 (apply after wayland-decorations.patch).

X11: keep XIM focus on the input context window across window manager
focus changes and input method restarts; keep commits made while the next
syllable is composing; a nested popup's field keeps the input method while
its parent popup's field is still editing.
Wayland: re-enable text input after every enter for the latest editor on
the focused surface or its popups; per-window requests and caret rectangles;
keyboard-based window focus across all seats.

Known limits:
- Wayland: preedit and commit are delivered to the seat's text input owner;
  with several seats typing into different popups at once, the IME target is
  not carried per seat through delivery.
- X11: preedit updates reach controls through a deferred notification, after
  the key events of the same batch (stock behaviour). A LineEdit given Enter
  while a syllable is composing then applies the stale preedit and inserts
  that syllable twice; the terminal is not affected. Notifying synchronously
  on commit fixes this but lets a parent popup's field take X focus back
  from a nested popup. Queueing preedit snapshots in X event order would fix
  both.
- X11: closing a nested popup returns X focus to the main window under
  metacity, which closes the parent popup too (stock Godot does the same).

